<section id="10006_S000J" variety="S000J">
<name>Engine Control</name>
<ttl id="10006_S000J_74WIJ_T00FO" variety="T00FO">
<name>EFI System (2GR-FE)</name>
<para id="RM000003D4E000X" category="C" type-id="3052C" name-id="066NL-00" from="200708">
<dtccode>P0017/59</dtccode>
<dtcname>Exhaust VVT Sensor (Out of Range)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0019/59</dtccode>
<dtcname>Exhaust VVT Sensor 2 (Out of Range)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000003D4E000X_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HS800000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>This VVT system performs advance and retard control of the intake and exhaust camshafts to provide optimal valve timing for each driving condition. This control is performed based on conditions such as intake air volume, throttle position and engine coolant temperature. Based on the signals from these sensors, the engine control computer adjusts the oil control valve so that the relative position of the camshaft becomes optimal, improving fuel economy, output and emission performance. The engine control computer also detects the actual valve timing using the signal from the camshaft position sensor and performs feedback control to achieve the target valve timing.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A145886J14" width="7.106578999in" height="4.7836529in"/>
</figure>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="0.94in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.78in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="2.36in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
<ptxt>SAE/TCCS</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Abnormal Condition</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Malfunction Duration</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Others</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Inspection Area</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>P0017/59</ptxt>
<ptxt>P0019/59</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="ordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Engine running</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Valve timing deviation (valve timing cannot be controlled to target)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>18 seconds or more</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>2 trip</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Mechanical system malfunction (timing chain jumped teeth, chain stretched)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>VVT signal (phase deviation)</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Engine Control Computer</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Camshaft timing oil control valve</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003D4E000X_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HS900000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A176822J05" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003D4E000X_03" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSA00000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>Read the freeze frame data using SST (TaSCAN). The freeze frame data records part of the engine operating condition when the malfunction occurred, and this information is useful when troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000003D4E000X_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSB00000">
<scantool type="2"/>
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the ignition ON and clear the DTCs following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0002" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSC00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Read DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the DTCs by following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Normal code is output</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0003" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0004" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0003">
<testtitle>Inspection for Intermittent Problems<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000CD101YX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSD00000">
<testtitle>Check for Rough Idle or Engine Stall</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the engine idle condition.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.63in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.08in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>DTC Output</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Vehicle Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>P0017/59</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Normal idle speed</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>P0019/59</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Normal idle speed</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>P0017/59 or P0019/59</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Engine stalls or idles roughly</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0005" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0007" fin="false">B</right>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0009" fin="false">C</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0005" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSE00000">
<scantool type="8"/>
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 1)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine stopped, turn the ignition ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [Active Test] - [Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 1].</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine idling, perform [Not Performed/Performed].</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.54in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.54in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Active Test (Oil Control Valve Condition)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Engine Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Performed (OCV operates)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Engine stalls or idles roughly</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Not performed (OCV does not operate)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Normal idle speed</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0006" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0009" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0006">
<testtitle>Replace Engine Control Computer<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002ADB004X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0007" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSF00000">
<scantool type="8"/>
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 2)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine stopped, turn the ignition ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [Active Test] - [Exhaust VVT Linear Drive Bank 2].</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine idling, perform [Not Performed/Performed].</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.54in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="3.54in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Active Test (Oil Control Valve Condition)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Engine Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Performed (OCV operates)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Engine stalls or idles roughly</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Not performed (OCV does not operate)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Normal idle speed</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0008" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0009" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0008">
<testtitle>Replace Engine Control Computer<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002ADB004X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0009" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSG00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Camshaft Timing Oil Control Valve Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Remove the camshaft timing oil control valve assembly (exhaust side).</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.86in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.14in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Terminal 1 - Terminal 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Approx. 20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>6.9 to 7.9Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A145883J05" width="2.775699831in" height="2.775699831in"/>
</figure>
<test1>
<ptxt>Operation Check</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Apply battery voltage between the terminals and check that the spool valve operates.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Operates</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Check that the spool valve is not stuck.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Poor return of the spool valve due to foreign matter such as sludge being caught may cause a slight pressure leak to the advance side, which may cause a DTC to be detected.</ptxt>
</atten4>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.08in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.05in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>OK</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>RH side malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>LH side malfunction</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>C</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0010" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0016" fin="true">B</right>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0017" fin="true">C</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0010" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSH00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Valve Timing</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Inspect Valve Timing</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Remove the cylinder head cover and cylinder head cover LH.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>Turn the crankshaft clockwise and align the notch of the crankshaft pulley with the 0° position.</ptxt>
</test2>
<test2>
<ptxt>As shown in the illustration, check that the timing marks of the camshaft timing gears are aligned. If the marks are not aligned, turn the crankshaft clockwise 1 more revolution.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A095456J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Timing marks are aligned</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0011" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0018" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0011" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSI00000">
<testtitle>Inspect Oil Control Valve Filter</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A135388J02" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<test1>
<ptxt>Remove oil pipe NO.1 or the oil pipe, and remove the oil control valve filter RH or LH.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the oil control valve filter for clogging.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>There is no clogging or adhering foreign matter</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0012" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0019" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0012" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSJ00000">
<testtitle>Inspect and Replace Oil Pipe</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Inspect and replace the oil pipe.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Check that the oil check valve bolt and oil pipe union are not clogged.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0013" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0013" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSK00000">
<scantool type="2"/>
<testtitle>Clear DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the ignition ON and clear the DTCs following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0014" fin="false">NEXT</down>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0014" proc-id="RM0550J___0000HSL00000">
<scantool type="1"/>
<testtitle>Read DTC</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="2">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Perform a road test.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check the DTCs by following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Normal code is output</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The DTC judgment can be checked using the [Check DTC Judgment Result] function of SST (TaSCAN). (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000008YS014X"/>)</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0015" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000003D4E000X_04_0020" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0015">
<testtitle>Inspection for Intermittent Problems<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000000CD101YX"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0016">
<testtitle>Replace Camshaft Timing Oil Control Valve Assembly (RH Bank, Exhaust Side)</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0017">
<testtitle>Replace Camshaft Timing Oil Control Valve Assembly (LH Bank, Exhaust Side)</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0018">
<testtitle>Valve Timing Adjustment</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0019">
<testtitle>Replace Oil Control Valve Filter</testtitle>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000003D4E000X_04_0020">
<testtitle>Replace Engine Control Computer<xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002ADB004X"/>
</testtitle>
</testgrp>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
